Chapter: BoundedParamTrap

 Bounded signatures, stage B (precondition): an out-of-range argument
 traps at the callee entry. feed threads 300 into inc-byte's parameter,
 which is bounded 0..255, and the entry guard traps with UD2.

 The __narrow is load-bearing and this test did not have it until
 2026-07-27, which is why it stopped compiling. Its prose used to say
 that 300 arriving through a plain-Integer parameter "is not a literal
 the static check could reject", and that was true when it was written.
 It is not now: CDX2051 refuses a bounded parameter whose argument has
 an unproven range, and refusing is the whole point -- the compiler will
 not silently insert a check you did not ask for. __narrow is how you
 ask, and its diagnostic says so.

Section: Definitions

  inc-byte : Integer between 0 and 255 -> Integer
  inc-byte (n) = n + 1

  feed : Integer -> Integer
  feed (x) = inc-byte (__narrow x)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (feed 300))
  end
